IMPORT prelude

-- Multimodal Transport Act 2021 (Singapore) -- when the Act applies (ss 2, 3), registering as a multimodal transport operator
-- (ss 4 to 6), the transport document as evidence (s 11), the operator's liability and its limits (ss 15, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23), the
-- consignor's dangerous-goods duties (s 24), notice of loss (s 25) and the time bar (s 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 23/9/2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MTA2021.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 17 of 2025 (Transport Sector (Miscellaneous
-- Amendments) Act 2025), in force 23 September 2026, which annotates s 11(2) and (3).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0102 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. A business meets this Act when it ships goods door to door across a border by two or more modes (say truck and
-- ship), or runs the freight-forwarding business that contracts to do so. Not encoded: the register itself and designated appeal
-- hearers (ss 7, 8), the issue and contents of the document and who may claim delivery (ss 9, 10, 14), the basis of valuation
-- (s 16), the mandatory-law limit for a localised loss (s 19), the servant-and-agent aggregate (s 22), arbitration (s 27),
-- void stipulations (s 28), general average and saved laws (ss 29, 30) and regulations (s 31). No regulations were retrieved, so
-- the prescribed fee, particulars and minimum assets are unknown. The Act creates no offences.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Multimodal Transport Act 2021 -- carriage of goods`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2 and 3 -- when the Act applies`

-- s 2(1): "international multimodal transport" is carriage under a multimodal transport contract "by at least 2 different modes of
-- transport" from a place in one country "to a place designated for the delivery of the goods situated in a different country".
-- "mode of transport" means "road, rail, inland waterways, sea or air". s 2(2): carriage "by only one mode of transport" is not
-- international multimodal transport.
-- s 3(1): Parts 3 to 6 apply to a civil claim only if the place for taking in charge, or the place for delivery, "as specified in
-- the contract is located in Singapore or an ASEAN member country"; (2) whether founded in contract or tort.
GIVEN `modes of transport used` IS A NUMBER, `delivery is in a different country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carriage is international multimodal transport` IF
    `modes of transport used` AT LEAST 2 AND `delivery is in a different country`

GIVEN `is international multimodal transport` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `taken in charge in Singapore or ASEAN` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `delivered in Singapore or ASEAN` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parts 3 to 6 apply to the claim` IF
    `is international multimodal transport` AND (`taken in charge in Singapore or ASEAN` OR `delivered in Singapore or ASEAN`)

§§ `4 to 6 -- registration certificate`

-- s 4(4): the Singapore competent national body "must not issue a registration certificate to an applicant unless the applicant" (a)
-- carries on or intends to carry on the business of international multimodal transport and is a company registered under the
-- Companies Act 1967 or has a business name registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014; (b) "has a principal place of
-- business in Singapore"; (c) has insurance, a bond, a guarantee or other acceptable financial arrangements covering claims for loss,
-- damage or delay; (d) "maintains the prescribed minimum assets, or provides an equivalent guarantee"; (e) meets other prescribed
-- requirements. These are conditions, not an entitlement: under s 4(3) the body "may" issue or refuse.
-- s 4(5): a certificate "is valid for one year". s 4(8), 5(6): appeal to the Minister "within 14 days of having been informed of the
-- refusal", whose decision "is final".
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `carries on or intends to carry on the business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a registered business name` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has its principal place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has acceptable insurance or financial cover` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the minimum assets or an equivalent guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the other prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body may issue a registration certificate` IF
        `the applicant`'s `carries on or intends to carry on the business`
    AND (`the applicant`'s `is a registered company` OR `the applicant`'s `has a registered business name`)
    AND `the applicant`'s `has its principal place of business in Singapore`
    AND `the applicant`'s `has acceptable insurance or financial cover`
    AND `the applicant`'s `has the minimum assets or an equivalent guarantee`
    AND `the applicant`'s `meets the other prescribed requirements`

-- s 5(1)(a): a renewal application must be made "at least 3 months before the date the registration certificate expires"; (2) one
-- submitted "less than 3 months before" expiry "is treated as an application under section 4".
GIVEN `months before expiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the renewal is treated as a fresh application` IF
    `months before expiry` LESS THAN 3

-- s 6(2), (3): before cancelling, the body must give notice and the time for written representations "must not be less than 28 days
-- after the date of the notice".
GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cancellation notice allows enough time` IF
    `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 28

-- s 6(6): appeal against cancellation "(a) within 14 days after being notified of the cancellation; or (b) if the holder requires
-- (within the period mentioned in paragraph (a)) the ... body to furnish the grounds of cancellation, within 14 days after being
-- furnished with the grounds". s 6(7): the cancellation "takes effect despite an appeal", unless the Minister otherwise specifies.
-- Days are counted as day numbers; reading "within 14 days after" as day + 14 is an inference.
GIVEN `day notified of cancellation` IS A NUMBER,
      `grounds requested within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `day grounds furnished` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to appeal the cancellation` MEANS
    IF `grounds requested within 14 days`
    THEN `day grounds furnished` PLUS 14
    ELSE `day notified of cancellation` PLUS 14

§§ `11 -- the transport document as evidence`

-- s 11(1): the document "is prima facie evidence that the multimodal transport operator has taken in charge the goods as described",
-- unless a contrary indication "such as 'shipper's weight, load and count', 'shipper-packed container' or a similar expression" is
-- on it. (2) [Act 17 of 2025]: "Proof to the contrary is not admissible" when the document has been transferred, or transmitted by
-- electronic data interchange, to the consignee who "(a) has acknowledged the receipt of the document; and (b) has in good faith
-- relied on and acted upon the document."
-- Read literally, (2) does not repeat the contrary-indication proviso of (1); this encoding assumes a qualified document is not
-- conclusive either (an inference).
GIVEN `bears a contrary indication` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `transferred to the consignee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consignee acknowledged receipt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consignee relied on it in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the description of the goods is conclusive against the operator` IF
        (NOT `bears a contrary indication`)
    AND `transferred to the consignee`
    AND `consignee acknowledged receipt`
    AND `consignee relied on it in good faith`

§§ `15 -- liability for loss, damage and delay`

-- s 15(1): the operator "is liable for loss resulting from the loss of, damage to, or delay in the delivery of" the goods if the
-- occurrence "took place during the period of responsibility" (s 12: from taking in charge until delivery).
-- (2) not liable if it proves (a) it, or those it answers for under s 13, "took all reasonable measures to avoid the occurrence", or
-- (b) the occurrence resulted from (i) force majeure; (ii) an act or neglect of the consignor or consignee; (iii) "insufficient or
-- defective packaging, marking or numbering"; (iv) handling, loading, unloading or stowage by the consignor or consignee; (v) "any
-- inherent or latent defect"; (vi) "any strike, lockout or stoppage or restraint of labour"; (vii) "where the goods are carried by
-- sea or inland waterways" -- (A) the master's or crew's "act, neglect or default ... in the navigation or in the management of the
-- ship", or (B) "any fire unless caused by the actual fault or privity of the carrier".
-- (3) not liable for delay "unless the consignor has made a declaration of interest in timely delivery which has been accepted".
-- (4) not liable for loss from unseaworthiness if it proves "due diligence has been exercised to make the ship seaworthy at the
-- commencement of the voyage".
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `force majeure`
    `an act of the consignor`
    `defective packaging`
    `stowage by the consignee's agent`
    `an inherent defect in the goods`
    `a port strike`
    `a navigation error by the master`
    `a fire not caused by the carrier's fault`
    `a fire caused by the carrier's actual fault`
    `careless handling by a subcontracted trucker`
    `no proven cause`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause, `the goods were at sea or on an inland waterway` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cause is an excepted cause` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `a navigation error by the master` THEN `the goods were at sea or on an inland waterway`
    WHEN `a fire not caused by the carrier's fault` THEN `the goods were at sea or on an inland waterway`
    WHEN `a fire caused by the carrier's actual fault` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `careless handling by a subcontracted trucker` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no proven cause` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `occurred during the period of responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is for delay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `delay interest declared and accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `operator proved all reasonable measures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proven cause` IS A Cause
    `at sea or on an inland waterway` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by unseaworthiness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `operator proved due diligence on seaworthiness` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator is liable` IF
        `the claim`'s `occurred during the period of responsibility`
    AND (NOT (`the claim`'s `is for delay` AND (NOT `the claim`'s `delay interest declared and accepted`)))
    AND (NOT `the claim`'s `operator proved all reasonable measures`)
    AND (NOT (`the cause is an excepted cause` (`the claim`'s `proven cause`) (`the claim`'s `at sea or on an inland waterway`)))
    AND (NOT (`the claim`'s `caused by unseaworthiness` AND `the claim`'s `operator proved due diligence on seaworthiness`))

-- s 15(5): delay occurs when the goods are not delivered within the agreed time or, failing agreement, a reasonable time. (6): "If
-- the goods have not been delivered within 90 consecutive days after the date determined in accordance with subsection (5)", the
-- person entitled may "treat the goods as lost". Reading "not delivered within 90 days" as "more than 90 days have passed" is an
-- inference.
GIVEN `has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN, `days past the delivery date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods may be treated as lost` IF
    (NOT `has been delivered`) AND `days past the delivery date` GREATER THAN 90

§§ `2(3), 17, 18, 20, 21 and 23 -- limits on liability, in SDR`

-- s 2(3): where a container, pallet or similar article is loaded with more than one package, "each of the packages or shipping units
-- enumerated in a multimodal transport document as packed in such article ... is considered a separate package"; "otherwise such
-- article of transport is considered the package".
GIVEN `packages enumerated in the document` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the packages counted` MEANS
    IF `packages enumerated in the document` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `packages enumerated in the document` ELSE 1

-- s 17(1): not liable "in an amount exceeding the higher of" (a) "666.67 SDR per package or shipping unit" or (b) "2.00 SDR per
-- kilogram of gross weight". s 18: if the contract "does not provide for the carriage of goods by sea or inland waterways", liability
-- "is limited to an amount not exceeding 8.33 SDR per kilogram". s 17(1) is expressly "subject to" s 18, so this encoding reads s 18
-- as REPLACING the s 17 limit for a land-and-air contract (no per-package alternative).
GIVEN `packages` IS A NUMBER, `kilograms` IS A NUMBER, `the contract provides for sea or inland waterway carriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the limit for goods lost or damaged` MEANS
    IF `the contract provides for sea or inland waterway carriage`
    THEN `the larger of` (666.67 TIMES `packages`) (2 TIMES `kilograms`)
    ELSE 8.33 TIMES `kilograms`

-- s 17(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the nature and value of the goods have been declared by the consignor ... before the
-- goods are taken in charge ... and inserted in the multimodal transport document." s 18 has no such carve-out: read literally, a
-- declared value lifts the s 17 limit but NOT the s 18 limit.
-- s 23(1): the operator loses "the benefit of the limitation of liability under this Part" if the loss "resulted from an act or
-- omission of the multimodal transport operator" done "(a) with the intention to cause such loss" or "(b) recklessly and with
-- knowledge that such loss ... would probably result". (s 19, a mandatory-law limit for a localised stage, is not encoded.)
GIVEN `the value of the loss` IS A NUMBER,
      `packages` IS A NUMBER,
      `kilograms` IS A NUMBER,
      `the contract provides for sea or inland waterway carriage` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `value declared in the document` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `operator's own intentional or reckless act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for loss or damage` MEANS
    IF `operator's own intentional or reckless act` THEN `the value of the loss`
    ELSE IF `value declared in the document` AND `the contract provides for sea or inland waterway carriage` THEN `the value of the loss`
         ELSE `the smaller of` `the value of the loss` (`the limit for goods lost or damaged` `packages` `kilograms` `the contract provides for sea or inland waterway carriage`)

-- s 20: liability "for loss resulting from delay in the delivery of the goods ... or any consequential loss or damage (other than loss
-- of or damage to the goods), is limited to an amount equivalent to the freight under the contract". With s 15(3): nothing for delay
-- unless a declaration of interest in timely delivery was accepted.
GIVEN `the delay loss` IS A NUMBER,
      `the freight` IS A NUMBER,
      `declaration of interest accepted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `operator's own intentional or reckless act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for delay` MEANS
    IF NOT `declaration of interest accepted` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `operator's own intentional or reckless act` THEN `the delay loss`
         ELSE `the smaller of` `the delay loss` `the freight`

-- s 21: "The aggregate liability ... must not exceed the limits of liability for the total loss of the goods ... calculated in
-- accordance with sections 17 and 18."
GIVEN `goods compensation` IS A NUMBER,
      `delay compensation` IS A NUMBER,
      `the limit for total loss` IS A NUMBER,
      `operator's own intentional or reckless act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate compensation` MEANS
    IF `operator's own intentional or reckless act` THEN `goods compensation` PLUS `delay compensation`
    ELSE `the smaller of` (`goods compensation` PLUS `delay compensation`) `the limit for total loss`

-- s 23(1) strips the operator's limit for an act "of the multimodal transport operator"; s 23(2) strips a servant's, agent's or
-- subcontractor's limit for THEIR intentional or reckless act. The heading speaks of a "personal act or omission". Read literally,
-- a servant's reckless act -- for which the operator is liable under s 13 -- does not cost the operator its own limit.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `the operator itself`
    `a servant or agent of the operator`
    `a subcontractor the operator used`

GIVEN `who acted` IS AN Actor, `with intent or reckless knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator loses its limit` IF
    `with intent or reckless knowledge` AND
        CONSIDER `who acted`
        WHEN `the operator itself` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `24 -- dangerous goods`

-- s 24(3): a consignor handing over dangerous goods "must inform" the operator "of the dangerous character of the goods and, if
-- necessary, the precautions to be taken". (4): if it fails to, "and the multimodal transport operator does not otherwise have
-- knowledge", (a) the consignor is liable for the operator's loss related to the dangerous character, and (b) "despite section 15"
-- the goods may be "unloaded, destroyed or rendered innocuous ... without payment of compensation". (5): (4) does not apply if the
-- operator "has taken in charge the goods with knowledge of the dangerous character".
-- (6): otherwise, if the goods "become an actual danger to life or property" they may be so dealt with without compensation,
-- "except where (a) there is an obligation ... to contribute in general average; or (b)" the operator "failed to take all reasonable
-- measures to prevent the dangerous goods becoming an actual danger".
GIVEN `consignor informed the operator` IS A BOOLEAN, `operator otherwise knew` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignor is liable for dangerous-goods losses` IF
    (NOT `consignor informed the operator`) AND (NOT `operator otherwise knew`)

GIVEN `consignor informed the operator` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `operator otherwise knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the goods became an actual danger` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `general average contribution owed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `operator failed to take reasonable measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods may be destroyed without compensation` IF
        `the consignor is liable for dangerous-goods losses` `consignor informed the operator` `operator otherwise knew`
    OR  (    `the goods became an actual danger`
         AND (NOT `general average contribution owed`)
         AND (NOT `operator failed to take reasonable measures`))

§§ `25 and 26 -- notice of loss and the time bar`

-- s 25(1): unless written notice of loss or damage "is given by the consignee ... when the goods were handed over", the handing-over
-- "is prima facie evidence of the delivery ... of the goods as described". (2): where the loss or damage "is not apparent", the
-- notice may be given "within 6 consecutive days after the day when the goods were handed over".
-- Day 0 is the day of handover.
GIVEN `the damage was apparent` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after handover the notice was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `handover is prima facie evidence of sound delivery` IF
    IF NOT `notice given` THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `the damage was apparent` THEN `days after handover the notice was given` GREATER THAN 0
         ELSE `days after handover the notice was given` GREATER THAN 6

-- s 26: "Unless otherwise expressly agreed", no court or arbitral action may be brought unless instituted (a) "within a period of 9
-- months after the delivery"; or (b) if not delivered, within 9 months "(i) after the date on which the goods should have been
-- delivered; or (ii) after the date on which, in accordance with section 15(6), failure to deliver the goods would give the consignee
-- ... the right to treat the goods as lost". Because (b) offers both starting points, the later one (90 days after the due date)
-- governs in practice. Only the default period is encoded; an express agreement otherwise (which the text does not limit to a
-- longer period) is not.
GIVEN `goods delivered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since delivery` IS A NUMBER,
      `months since the due date` IS A NUMBER,
      `months since the goods could be treated as lost` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is in time` IF
    IF `goods delivered` THEN `months since delivery` AT MOST 9
    ELSE `months since the due date` AT MOST 9 OR `months since the goods could be treated as lost` AT MOST 9
